  "title": "Nowakowska Theory of Actions (1982) in Lean 4",
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib (v4.36.0-rc2) formalization of Maria Nowakowska's A Formal Theory of Actions (Syntax and Semantics of Behaviour; chapter dated 1982; Praxiological Studies, 1983), synthesizing the parts of Language of Motivation and Language of Actions (1973) that 1982 cites for omitted proofs and for the motivational calculus (here: §§2.1.4, 2.2.4, 5.1–5.3). Framing: rigorous reconstruction/verification of her action–motivation–promise material (precision gaps closed in Lean), plus a formalization contribution proving CF ∩ Regular so Promise/Offense CF theorems are unconditional. Headline compared claims include card_conflictFamilies (her stated 113), Attainable_iff_reaches_length (reachability realization), arrow_impossibility in the finite 2×3 encoding, unconditional PromiseClosed/OffenseClosed.isContextFree with factor-minimal HatU, Language.IsContextFree.inter_regular, and stringDuration_pi / timed ψ-membership. Clinical Arrow abbrevs and MotCalc samples are supporting packaging, not claimed novelty. Maria Nowakowska did not participate in or endorse this formalization. Lean was written with AI-agent assistance under Lars Warren Ericson's direction and review. There is no sorry in the Actions/ development, no project-defined axiom, and Mathlib is the only Lake dependency. Palomar Registration: TBD.",
